.TH LIBMONGOOSE_J2534 7 "September 2026" "mongoose-j2534 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
libmongoose_j2534 \- J2534 pass-thru library for the MongoosePro JLR adapter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <mongoose/j2534.h>
.B cc app.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs mongoose-j2534)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
An unofficial SAE J2534-1 04.04 pass-thru library for the MongoosePro JLR USB adapter (18e1:0104). It exports
.BR PassThruOpen ,
.BR PassThruClose ,
.BR PassThruConnect ,
.BR PassThruDisconnect ,
.BR PassThruReadMsgs ,
.BR PassThruWriteMsgs ,
.BR PassThruStartPeriodicMsg ,
.BR PassThruStopPeriodicMsg ,
.BR PassThruStartMsgFilter ,
.BR PassThruStopMsgFilter ,
.BR PassThruSetProgrammingVoltage ,
.BR PassThruReadVersion ,
.B PassThruGetLastError
and
.BR PassThruIoctl .
It reaches the adapter through the kernel's cdc_acm serial port, so it needs no vendor software, libusb or root.
.PP
Raw CAN and 11-bit ISO15765 are implemented, with multi-frame receive and transmit, pass, block and flow-control
filters, periodic messages, configuration, loopback and the buffer IOCTLs. K-line, J1850, the pin-switched
protocols, 29-bit ISO15765 and programming-voltage output return
.BR ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED .
.PP
.B Use it at your own risk.
It is unofficial, has been tested on one vehicle and one adapter, and comes with no warranty. It can send anything
to a vehicle's networks and does not guard against harmful requests.
.SH DEVICE NAMES
The name given to
.B PassThruOpen
is
.B NULL
(the single connected adapter),
.BI serial: S\fR,
.BI tty: "[serial:S|/dev/ttyACMn]"
or
.BI usb: "[serial:S]"
(libusb, if built in). One process at a time may hold the adapter; another gets
.BR ERR_DEVICE_IN_USE .
Only one CAN-family channel can be open on the adapter.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/ttyACM*
The adapter's serial port.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-mongoose-j2534.rules
Grants the active seat user access and keeps ModemManager from probing the port.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mongoose_j2534/USING.md
The full usage guide: channels, ISO15765 requirements, IOCTLs and configuration parameters, errors.
.SH ABI
Symbols are versioned
.BR MONGOOSE_0 ;
the soname is
.BR libmongoose_j2534.so.0 .
The 14 exported functions and the structures in the header are stable within a soname; nothing else is exported.
.SH THREADS
Calls may be made from several threads. Commands to one adapter are serialised. A blocked
.B PassThruReadMsgs
or timed
.B PassThruWriteMsgs
is woken by
.B PassThruDisconnect
or
.BR PassThruClose
on its channel. The text returned by
.B PassThruGetLastError
is per thread. Behaviour across
.BR fork (2)
is not defined and was not tested: open the adapter in the process that uses it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mongoose-client (1),
.BR mongoose-diag (1),
.BR mongoose-socketcan (1)
